<h2 class="section-title">About Pykara Lake Boat House</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-6">Pykara Lake Boat House is the lake-boating destination near Ooty in the Nilgiris, Tamil Nadu. The Nilgiris District Administration describes the lake as about 21 km from Ooty on the Ooty–Mysore road. Its destination page mentions boating and a restaurant, but is marked updated 16 July 2018: it is background, not a current facilities or operating audit.</p><p class="prose-copy mt-4">Pykara is a different booking location from Ooty Boat House. Select Pykara, your travel date and the desired boat type on TTDC’s official booking portal. Check the final fare, availability, included services and cancellation terms before payment. This independent guide does not sell tickets or confirm a sailing.</p>
<h2 class="section-title mt-12">Location &amp; How to Visit Pykara Lake</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-6">The supplied Maps listing describes Pykara, Naduvattam, Tamil Nadu. A government tourism directory uses a different Plus Code and administrative label, so this guide does not turn either code into a guaranteed entrance. Ask TTDC for the boat house approach and drop-off, then plan from your actual starting point.</p><p class="prose-copy mt-4">For a bus journey, check the relevant operator’s current outbound and return services and the stop serving the boat house. A bus along the main road does not establish a direct entrance stop or a usable final walking connection. For a taxi, agree the fare, waiting arrangements and return pickup. Approximate distance is not a travel-time promise.</p>
<h2 class="section-title mt-12">Landmarks &amp; Attractions Around Pykara Lake</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-6">Pykara Falls is a separate visit with its own approach and access conditions. The district tourism page also describes Wenlock Downs in the wider Pykara route context. Check current entry, permission, route and weather for each stop; this guide does not promise an easy half-day circuit or combine lake and falls admission.</p>
<h2 class="section-title mt-12">History &amp; Significance of Pykara</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-6">The district account identifies the river’s source at Mukurthi and records its significance to the Toda community. Treat that cultural significance respectfully and follow local directions; it is not an invitation to enter sacred or restricted areas. The boat house, lake and waterfalls should be understood as related but distinct visitor locations.</p><p class="prose-copy mt-4">For operational information, TTDC’s official app lists Pykara among its boat-house booking destinations and offers date/boat-type selection. Neither that listing nor the district background page verifies a universal daily timetable or a fixed fare for every visitor.</p><p class="mt-5 text-sm"><a class="underline font-bold" href="https://nilgiris.nic.in/tourist-place/pykara-ooty/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">District primary source ↗</a> · <a class="underline font-bold" href={ATTRACTION.operatorUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official TTDC booking ↗</a></p>
</div><aside class="card p-6 self-start"><h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">Access needs: ask before travel</h3><p class="prose-copy mt-4">The 29 October 2026 Google Maps listing snapshot reported no accessible entrance. It is a third-party listing observation, not an on-site access survey. Ask about the complete journey from vehicle drop-off to boarding, steps, gradients, toilets, assistance and a suitable boat before relying on access.</p><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-7">Hours are not yet confirmed</h3><p class="prose-copy mt-3">A 30 October 2026 Madras High Court order set the lake’s visitor window at 10:00–16:00 and requires managed booking with daily visitor-capacity limits. Ask TTDC separately about counter opening, last departure, access to the lake area and operation on your travel date. No other recurring timetable is inferred from older tourism material.</p></aside></div></div></section>
